X86 SB+tsavorite
(* Tsavorite's per-operation double-announce (Resume/Acquire announce +
 * InternalRefresh/ProtectAndDrain announce), on x86-TSO.
 *
 *   x = the reader's announce slot   (localCurrentEpoch)
 *   y = the object's linked flag     (curPage != 0)
 *
 * P0 = reader     : TWO plain announce STOREs (x=1, x=1) ; then LOAD the flag (y).
 * P1 = reclaimer  : STORE unlink (y=1) ; then LOAD the scan (x).
 *
 * Even with the doubled announce, x86-TSO still allows StoreLoad reordering, so
 * the `exists` outcome (both loads read 0) is Sometimes -- the window exists in
 * the abstract. In Tsavorite specifically it is nonetheless masked in practice:
 * TryAcquireEntry's Interlocked.CompareExchange runs (a full fence) on the same
 * per-operation hot path, draining the store buffer before the load (see the
 * README, sections 2.1 and 8). *)
{ }
 P0            | P1            ;
 MOV [x],$1    | MOV [y],$1    ;
 MOV [x],$1    | MOV EAX,[x]   ;
 MOV EBX,[y]   |               ;
exists
(0:EBX=0 /\ 1:EAX=0)
